Real work the agent finishes stays finished: it plans a goal, makes two edits
it can show, and closes the goal. The judge that reads the end of the
conversation finds it met, and does not send the agent back to redo it.

-- project/greet.go --
package main

import "fmt"

func main() { fmt.Println("hello") }
-- prompt --
Plan this as a goal with steps, then do all of it now: make greet.go print "hello, world" instead of "hello", and add a README.md that says to run it with `go run greet.go`.
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
file greet.go contains hello, world
file README.md contains go run greet.go
mem-count open == 0
mem-count done >= 1
cmd ! grep -q "found not met" .gnosh/logs/gnosh.log
